    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d649">

                <pb facs="0778" n="690" sameAs="frus:frus1904/pg690"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hay to Mr. Dudley.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1904-04-11"><hi rendition="#italic">April 11,
                        1904</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 325.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have to acknowledge the receipt of your
                    No. 879, of the 5th ultimo, reporting that you had pointed out to the Peruvian
                    minister of foreign relations the inability of the United States legation and
                    consulates to give the certificate required by a recent supreme decree,
                    providing that foreigners desiring to marry in Peru must furnish a certificate
                    of celibacy from their legation or consulate.</p>
                <p>The views expressed by you are correct and are approved by the Department.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">John Hay.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
